#!/usr/bin/env bash
set -euo pipefail
cat >&2 <<'EOF'
bdus — deployment toolbox for this BraDypUS install

  bdus <command> [instance|all] [args]

Setup (one-time, needs sudo)
  setup host              host prep: docker group, daemon.json, ufw, DOCKER-USER
                          firewall + systemd unit, /srv/bradypus, unattended-upgrades

Instances
  init <instance>         create /srv/bradypus/<instance> from config.env
                          (bradypus.yml + .env + bdus.override.yml), pull, up, wait healthy
  status                  one-screen health of every instance (exit != 0 if anything is wrong)
  update <inst|all> <ver> pull & switch to <ver>: checks the tag exists on GHCR, backs up
                          prod first, verifies the instance comes back, reverts the pin if not
  start | stop | restart <inst|all>
  pull <inst|all>         pre-fetch images without restarting
  logs <instance> [...]   docker compose logs, passthrough

Data
  backup [inst|all]       data/projects tar; pg instance also pg_dumpall; martin instance also
                          gis-data tar. Prunes to BACKUP_RETENTION, rsyncs off-box if set.
  restore <instance> [--db FILE] [--files FILE] [--yes]
                          stop api → restore (latest by default) → start api

Applications
  app add    <instance> --name <slug> --engine sqlite|pgsql --email <admin> [--db-name X]
                          [--gis] [--gis-write]   (pgsql: provision PostGIS/Martin/QGIS roles too)
  app gis    <instance> <app> [--write]   add/retrofit PostGIS + Martin/QGIS roles on an existing app
  app list   [inst|all]
  app export <instance> <app> [--out FILE]      one portable archive (tree + pg_dump)
  app import <instance> <archive> [--force] [--new-jwt]   the reverse, incl. into another instance
  app delete <instance> <app> [--yes] [--no-backup] [--keep-role]   exports first, then removes

Vector tiles (optional, per instance)
  INSTANCE_<n>_MARTIN=1 in config.env (+ _MARTIN_PORT) adds a Martin service for
  serving tiles from geodata kept outside BraDypUS (e.g. QGIS) — see `app gis` above
  to attach an app to it, and DEPLOY-RUNBOOK.md §18 for the rest.

Diagnostics
  doctor                  check the deploy invariants (.env perms, override, firewall rules,
                          bradypus-fw.service, cron, rsync target)

Config: config.env (copy from config.env.example). Runbook: DEPLOY-RUNBOOK.md.
EOF
